      "writtenOn": "2022-05-17T20:27:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This actually breaks the current colorizer when there\u0027s a hard stop at 1, since the t passed into colorize_grad_4 is never \u003e1.\n\nThe most straightforward fix for that might be to just take this clamp out and assume the current behavior of the colorizer. But, I have reservations about the colorizer implementation anyways since it does some divide-by-zeros on hard stops, which I guess is undefined behavior. I do like that the colorizer avoids branching but I\u0027m not sure if there\u0027s any way around introducing some conditional logic to avoid dividing by zero there?",
      "revId": "4615ce526c0e95a9ad517c64f19edf1a649b7a3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce2a54d7_601da959",
        "filename": "src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 75,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-17T20:48:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A hard stop at 1 is meaningless, right? `build_intervals` in GrGradientShader.cpp already has code which eliminates empty intervals; Graphite probably needs to do something similar if it doesn\u0027t already:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/gradients/GrGradientShader.cpp;l\u003d357-363?q\u003dbuild_intervals",
      "parentUuid": "e21352f8_2f8b8cbe",
      "revId": "4615ce526c0e95a9ad517c64f19edf1a649b7a3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0a52aeb_048e40a9",
        "filename": "src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 75,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-17T20:53:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I understand, hard stops at 0 or 1 are only meaningful when you\u0027re clamping. In that case any point before or after the gradient \"bounds\" will have the color from the hard stop. So the issue here is that when we have a hard stop at 1 and we\u0027re coloring pixels at t \u003e 1, the hard stop at 1 isn\u0027t taken into effect.",
      "parentUuid": "ce2a54d7_601da959",
      "revId": "4615ce526c0e95a9ad517c64f19edf1a649b7a3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9aed00a2_2b8d799c",
        "filename": "src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl",
